.PP
\fBpmap\fR matches procps-ng's behaviour on the supported flag set —
default, device (\fB\-d\fR), and extended (\fB\-x\fR) formats; their
quiet (\fB\-q\fR) variants; and the multi-PID layout. Some procps-ng
features are not yet implemented:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-X\fR / \fB\-XX\fR — "extra extended" formats that surface
arbitrary \fIsmaps\fR fields as columns. The plain \fB\-x\fR format
covers the common Kbytes/RSS/Dirty case.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-c\fR / \fB\-C\fR / \fB\-n\fR / \fB\-N\fR — alternate config-file
selection flags. \fBpmap\fR does not consult a config file.
.PP
Error messages for invalid arguments use different wording.
